# 7. REST API Specification

Use versioned endpoints under:

`https://your-domain.com/api/v1/`

## 7.1 Device Authentication

POST `/devices/pair`

Purpose:
- Pair the kiosk with the backend.
- Exchange a one-time administrator-issued pairing code for a device credential.

POST `/devices/heartbeat`

Purpose:
- Verify device registration.
- Report application and connection status.

The kiosk must have a revocable device token.

Store device credentials securely in app-private storage, preferably protected using Android Keystore where supported.

Never embed a shared administrator password or R2 credential in the application.

## 7.2 Upload Endpoints

POST `/events/{eventId}/videos/initiate`

Request:
- kiosk_video_id
- duration_seconds
- file_size
- mime_type
- width
- height
- checksum, if supported

Response:
- cloud_video_id
- upload_url
- upload_headers
- upload_expires_at
- expected_file_size

POST `/videos/{videoId}/complete`

Purpose:
- Verify uploaded object.
- Check object existence.
- Verify file size and expected content type.
- Finalize upload.
- Generate QR token.
- Return viewing URL.

POST `/videos/{videoId}/upload-failed`

Purpose:
- Record an upload failure.
- Store the error category.
- Allow later retry.

GET `/videos/{videoId}/status`

Purpose:
- Reconcile upload state after connection interruptions.

## 7.3 Home Feed Endpoints

GET `/events/{eventId}/videos`

Parameters:
- cursor
- limit

Return:
- Available videos for the event
- Metadata
- Thumbnail information
- Expiration date

Sort by newest first.

Use cursor-based pagination.

The server must never return videos belonging to a different event.

## 7.4 QR Viewing Endpoints

GET `/v/{token}`

Purpose:
- Resolve the unique access token.
- Verify the video is AVAILABLE.
- Verify it has not expired.
- Render the mobile video-viewing page.

GET `/api/v1/public/videos/{token}/playback`

Purpose:
- Validate the QR token.
- Generate a short-lived presigned GET URL.
- Return playback information.

GET `/api/v1/public/videos/{token}/download`

Purpose:
- Validate the token.
- Generate a short-lived download URL.
- Use an appropriate Content-Disposition attachment response.

The public viewing page must not expose R2 credentials or database IDs.

## 7.5 Admin Endpoints

GET `/admin/events/{eventId}/videos`

GET `/admin/events/{eventId}/storage`

DELETE `/admin/videos/{videoId}`

POST `/admin/videos/{videoId}/rotate-token`

POST `/admin/videos/{videoId}/retry-verification`

GET `/admin/uploads`

